1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Michiko''' is a member of the Imperial House of Japan. She was Empress of Japan as the wife of Akihito, the 125th Emperor of Japan reigning from 7 January 1989 to 30 April 2019.
2 CONT
2 CONT Michiko married Crown Prince Akihito and became Crown Princess of Japan in 1959. She was the first commoner to marry into the Japanese imperial family. She has three children with her husband: Naruhito, Fumihito, and Sayako. Her e
2 CONC lder son, Naruhito, is the current emperor. As crown princess and later as empress consort, she has become the most visible and widely travelled imperial consort in Japanese history. Upon Akihito's abdication, Michiko received the
2 CONC  new title of Jōkōgō (上皇后), or Empress Emerita. ''(Wikipedia, CC BY-SA 4.0)''
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empress_Michiko Wikipedia: Empress Michiko]
